{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>And the first came out ruddy, all of him like a hairy mantle, etc.</b> This was a sign that he would be a deceitful hunter, to deceive his father in the manner of hypocrites who present themselves as modest. And along the lines of what is said for the future (Zechariah 13:4): ״וְלֹא יִלְבְּשׁוּ אַדֶּרֶת שֵׂעָר לְמַעַן כַּחֵשׁ״ — for such was the custom in that time, that the modest would wear a hairy mantle, and perhaps even in the days of Isaac the custom was so. Therefore he was born like a hairy mantle, to say that he would be a nazir of Elohim from the womb and would belong to the sect of hypocrites. This is also a sign for him that he would be a shepherd of whores, for the sign for that is that his hairs are large, as the Rambam wrote in Hilkhot De'ot (ch. 4, hal. 19)." "<b>And they called his name Esau.</b> For he was made and completed in his hair — this is a sign that this world would be his portion and lot, and he would have no portion in the eternal world. For the distinction between the acquisition of these two kinds of perfection is this: immediately when a person is born, he makes use of all the physical instruments, and all five senses perform their function, and immediately he has desire and longing for all the lusts that matter craves and covets — eating and drinking and the rest of the body's necessary functions. But in the intellectual instruments, such as the brain and the heart and the intellect itself, a person does not make use of them at all on the day of his birth, for עַיִר פֶּרֶא יִוָּלֵד אָדָם (Job 11:12). But as he advances in years, the eye of his intellect opens and he acquires this superior perfection little by little, as we explained in parashat Bereshit on the verse ״וַיְהִי הָאָדָם לְנֶפֶשׁ חַיָּה״ (Genesis 2:7). And according to this, the fact that Esau was born completed in his hair is a proof that all his primary uses would be with the instruments of matter — those made and completed at the time of birth — and they do not add in their essence any increase."], :book :genesis, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:30:08.294422619Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}